Item 13 is done, and with it the loop: 13 of 13 items are solved and `LOOP_COMPLETE` is the last line of PROGRESS.md. The gate passes: `lake build` succeeds, the only `sorry` is still the §24 conjecture, and pytest reports 1327 passed, 2 skipped and 1 expected failure.

**Result.** The repaired definite move is equivalent to a simple matching test, not just implied by it. Item 08 had proved that the test is enough to make the move sound, and had only checked the other direction by brute force. That converse is now proved in Lean. So if the test fails at a node, the repaired move really does fail there. The solver fix you decided on can use one bipartite matching per candidate and lose nothing against the full repair.

**Lean.** The new file `lean/MOSPFormalization/Search/DefiniteMatching.lean` (about 200 lines) has no `sorry`. Its axioms are only `propext`, `Classical.choice` and `Quot.sound`, which I added to the audit in `paper2/axiom_check.lean`. The main theorem is `isHereditarilyDefinite_iff_hasDefiniteMatching`, which holds for every state and customer. The proof gives each candidate the same handful of dummy stacks, applies Mathlib's Hall theorem (`Finset.all_card_le_biUnion_card_iff_existsInjective'`), and keeps the customers matched to real stacks.

**Python check.** I ran it before stating the theorem: `python -m paper2.search_check --hall` takes 7 s. It covers every state, not only free-closed ones, on every graph up to 7 vertices, plus 1,000 random graphs on 10–12 vertices and both counterexample graphs. There were zero failures across 15.2 M checks of the equivalence and 70.3 M checks of the supporting lemmas. Five new tests are in `tests/test_search_check.py`. They include two deliberate faults planted in the checker, and the tests catch both.

**Docs.** `paper2/search_soundness.md` has a new §4.6, and §2.2, §4.2.4 and §5.5 no longer say the equivalence is unproved. `DefiniteMove.lean` still says "checked, not proved here". I left that alone because the loop's rules forbid editing proved Lean files, and it is still true of that file.

